      "message": "A good way of writing this is to split it across multiple lines\n\n    0x6 \u003c\u003c 28 // Ip version\n    + CONSTANT_NAME \u003c\u003c 16 // traffic class\n\nYou could even give these constants names if you find this more readable\n\n    IP_FAMILY \u003d 6 \u003c\u003c 28\n    TRAFFIC_CLASS \u003d 2 \u003c\u003c 16\n    putInt(IP_FAMILY + TRAFFIC_CLASS)\n\nBut in this case, considering the buf is big endian anyway I think it\u0027s most readable if you say something like\n\n    buf.put((byte) 6 \u003c\u003c 8); // IP version\n    buf.put((byte) 2); // traffic class\n    buf.putShort((short) 0); // flow label",
