      "lineNbr": 745,
      "author": {
        "id": 1304263
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-14T14:42:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not really. NattKeepalivePacketData.nattKeepalivePacket() is not allowed v6 addresses. Taking a v6 address will cause an exception. We remove the constraint in NattKeepalivePacketData to allow taking a v6 address, but I think we should make the change specific to clat case. In v6 ony without clat or dual stack cases, we do not need to do the translation. (though I think a v4 keepalive request should not be started).\n\nI think this check make the behavior change smaller. \n\nDesign is also updated. See if it make sense to you.",
      "parentUuid": "0bc21b48_e2de7d16",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 744,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 745,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "388f2cd3bca411b98e14ab5241d4fb1016b4cdfc",
